"For some fixed positive integer $n$, let $\\Delta\\subset \\mathbb{R}^n$ be a rational simplex. The **simplex Polytope Translation hardness conjecture.** For some fixed $n$, the Polytope Translation problem for rational simplices $\\Delta\\subset \\mathbb{R}^n$ is ${\\textup{\\textsf{NP}}}$-hard. This is proposed as a stronger simplification of the general polytope hardness result, and the source leaves it open."